schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Cooperative Economics and Digital Commons
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: framework
  summary: >-
    Explains cooperative economics (worker, consumer, savings-and-loan, and
    multi-stakeholder cooperatives) grounded in Somaliland/East African
    traditions (coffee cooperatives, savings circles), extends the idea to
    the digital commons and DAOs, walks through Elinor Ostrom's eight
    principles for governing shared resources, and lists funding paths
    (member contributions, savings-group formalization, grants, quadratic
    funding, community currencies).
  audience: community stewards in Somaliland/East Africa building cooperative or commons-based projects
  known_tensions:
    - informal-savings-circles-already-work vs formalizing-them-into-registered-cooperatives-with-broader-reach
  related_concepts:
    - ostroms-eight-principles
    - digital-commons
    - tokenization
  related_resources:
    - Mondragon Worker Cooperative Federation
    - Greenpill Network
    - Gitcoin Grants
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/cooperative-commons.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-d800b62ea134
  source_lineage: cooperative-commons.md
  notes: |
    # assessed-but-excluded
    - "target_audience: Somaliland / East Africa" in the source frontmatter names a
      region, not an exact location or individual/community profile, so no
      high-risk flag; kept as general geographic/cultural framing only.
